verses.text:
What the cutter left, the swarmer has eaten;
what the swarmer left, the hopper has eaten;
and what the hopper left, the stripper has eaten.{b}

It has turned my vine into a waste
and splintered my fig tree;
it has peeled it bare and thrown it down;
its branches are bleached white.

The fields are ruined;
the ground mourns;
for the grain is destroyed,
the new wine dries up,
the oil fails.

Hang your heads, you tillers of the soil;
howl, you who tend the vines,
for wheat and for barley,
since the field’s harvest is lost.

The vine has withered;
the fig tree droops;
pomegranate, palm, and apple,{d}
every tree of the field is dried up;
and gladness has withered away
from the children of mankind.

Alas for the day!
For the day of Yahweh is near,
and as destruction from the Almighty it comes.{e}

The seeds shrivel beneath the clods;{f}
the storehouses are desolate;
the granaries are torn down,
for the grain has dried up.

How the beasts groan!
The herds of cattle wander in confusion
because they have no pasture;
even the flocks of sheep are made to suffer.{g}

Like mighty men they run;
like men of war they climb the wall.
They march each in his own line;
they do not break their ranks.

Upon the city they spring;
along the wall they run;
into the houses they climb;
in through the windows they come like a thief.

Yahweh utters his voice
before his army,
for his host is exceedingly great;
mighty is he who carries out his word.
For the day of Yahweh is great and very fearsome;
who can endure it?

Rend your heart and not your garments,
and turn back to Yahweh your God;
for he is gracious and merciful,
slow to anger and great in steadfast love,
and he repents of the harm.{d}

Blow the horn in Zion;
set apart a fast;
call a solemn assembly;

Do not be afraid, O land;
be glad and rejoice,
for Yahweh has done great things!

Do not be afraid, you beasts of the field,
for the pastures of the wilderness are green;
the tree bears its fruit;
fig tree and vine yield their full strength.

“And afterward{i}
I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh;
your sons and your daughters will prophesy;
your old men will dream dreams,
and your young men will see visions.

I will assemble all the nations
and lead them down into the Valley of Jehoshaphat.{b}
There I will go to law with them
for my people and my inheritance Israel,
whom they dispersed among the nations;
and they parceled out my land.

Proclaim this among the nations:
Prepare for war;{f}
stir up the warriors.
Let all the fighting men draw near;
let them come up.

Hammer your plowshares into swords
and your pruning hooks into spears;{g}
let the weakling say, “I am a warrior.”

Hurry and come, all you nations round about;
gather yourselves there.
Bring down your warriors, Yahweh!

I will avenge their blood,
which I have not yet avenged;{j}
for Yahweh dwells in Zion.”
